  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Above normal temperatures, at least 5 to 10\ndegrees above average, expected Tuesday through late week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA large high pressure system will move east across the Mid \nAtlantic coast and out to sea on Tuesday. Areas to the N of the \nhigh will be influence by the WSW flow. This will bring mostly \nsunny skies and warm temps, at least 5 to 10 degrees above \nnormal for this time of year. However, the SW flow will keep \ncoastal temps much lower due to the sea breeze. The hot \nweather, combined with some modest instability and weak low \npressure waves moving through the area, should also help to \ndevelop some isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms \neach afternoon beginning Wednesday and continuing through the \nend of the week. No severe potential is expected at this time \ndue to the limited instability.",
